{"name":"Ethereal Dance","hex":"#1a4a5a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ethereal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Pertaining to the presupposition of an invisible air-like element permeating all of space, or to the higher regions beyond the earth or beyond the atmosphere.","Pertaining to the immaterial realm, as symbolically represented by, or (in earlier epochs) conflated with, such atmospheric and extra-atmospheric concepts."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Ellipsis of ethereal wave (“music genre”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ethereal"},{"term":"dance","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sequence of rhythmic steps or movements usually performed to music, for pleasure or as a form of social interaction.","A social gathering where dancing is the main activity."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To move with rhythmic steps or movements, especially in time to music.","To leap or move lightly and rapidly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dance"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dance","blocks":[{"text":"Dance is an art form, consisting of sequences of body movements with aesthetic and often symbolic value, either improvised or purposefully selected. Dance can be categorized and described by its choreography, by its repertoire of movements or by its historical period or place of origin. Dance is typically performed with musical accompaniment, and sometimes with the dancer simultaneously using a musical instrument themselves."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Two_dancers.jpg/330px-Two_dancers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dance","wikidata":"Q11639"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/GDC_onlywayaround.jpg/500px-GDC_onlywayaround.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wi